    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="1426" n="1402" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg1402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot M–88: Box 2079: CFM
                    Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the United States Delegation to the
                        Council of Foreign Ministers</hi><anchor n="54" xml:id="d379-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> CFM(46)(NY)44</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-03"
                            >December 3, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peace Treaty With Italy: Free
                        Territory of Trieste</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">Protocol of . . . . .</p>
                <p>The representatives of France, U.S.S.R., U.K., and U.S.A., assembled on . . . . .
                    at New York as the Council of Foreign Ministers, have agreed that their
                    Governments will recommend to the General <pb facs="1427" n="1403"
                        xml:id="pg1403"/> Assembly of the United Nations during its present session,
                    the taking of the necessary steps to furnish to the Free Territory of Trieste
                    such sums as may, in the opinion of the General Assembly, be needed during the
                    first six months’ period <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) to meet the salary and
                    expenses of the Governor and any deficit in the administrative budget of the
                    Territory and <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) to make available the foreign
                    exchange resources required to meet any deficit on the Territory’s external
                    balance of payments, and will take all necessary measures to support such steps
                    in the United Nations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d379-f1" n="54" type="source" xml:id="d379-f1-content">
                <p>This paper was submitted by the Deputies to the Council of Foreign Ministers in
                    connection with the Deputies’ paper CFM(46) (NY)43, December 3, 1946, <ref
                        target="#pg1396">p. 1396</ref>; for a further description of the origin of
                    this paper, see the Report of the Deputies as recorded in the United States
                    Delegation Minutes of the 14th Meeting of the Council, December 3, <ref
                        target="#pg1382">p. 1382</ref>. After considering this paper at its 14th
                    Meeting, the Council referred it to the Trieste Sub-Committee for study and
                    recommendations; see the Record of Decisions of that Council meeting, <ref
                        target="#pg1400">p. 1400</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
